# Build output
x64/
Debug/
Release/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ipdb
*.iobj
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
*.tlog
*.log

# Generated by tools/build.ps1 step [3/5]: the whole DLL embedded as a C array,
# ~31 MB. Rebuilt from x64/Release/enhance.dll every time, so committing it would
# be committing a binary that is already in the repo as source.
injector/bytes.hpp

# A full copy of an older version of this project sitting inside itself (~279 MB).
enhance-client-main/

# Downloaded mapping artifacts for all 24 supported versions (~220 MB): Mojang
# ProGuard files, Fabric intermediary jars, and the pieces of the 26.x client jars
# that tools/mc_artifacts.py reads through range requests. All of it is fetched
# from published, immutable URLs and verified by sha1, so it is a cache and not a
# source. What IS committed is what the cache produces: tools/symbols/symbols.json
# and sdk/mappings/mappings_gen.inc, so a build with a cold cache still works.
tools/mappings/cache/

# IDE / local
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# Runtime
enhance_log.txt
crash-*.txt

# Python bytecode cache from the mapping tools.
__pycache__/
